R-AP23 R-AP45 R-AP34 R-AD35 R-DA1 R-DA5 R-DA8 R-AP9 R-AP10 R-RG3: http_send!, http_all! and sleep! with the fake Fx (tests/commands/L2Http.roc, entry http). The registry is http://127.0.0.1:9, the route form is the one of TESTING 3.1 (proposal of slice 200, see FakeFx.roc).
Runs 1 to 4 (R-AP23, R-AP45 client side): POST /v1/releases with Content-Type: application/json and User-Agent: tln/0.4.1 and a JSON body. The route has `require` lines for these 2 headers and `require-none authorization` (R-RG3). The Nth answer of one route: run 1 gives 201 (file .POST), run 2 gives 200 (.POST.2), run 3 gives 409 problem+json (.POST.3), run 4 has no .POST.4 and gives the first answer again. calls.log has the method, the URL, the timeout, the headers and the body line.
Run 5 (no header) and run 6 (with Authorization) break a require line: status 599 and the body `wrong header`. Run 7: GET of the same URL is the plain route (a body, not the POST route). Run 8 (PUT, a body with a new line): the log has the body on one line, `\n` escaped. Run 9 (DELETE): 204 and an empty body (R-AP36 to R-AP38 methods). Run 10: a route with no file: 404 for any method.
Runs 11 and 12: GET /v1/ping twice with http_send!: the 2nd request has the answer of .2. Run 13: the timeout in the log is the timeout of the request. Run 14: a route with `error timeout` gives Timeout.
Runs 15 and 16 (R-AD35 step 3, R-DA5, R-DA8): http_all! with limit 2 and 4 requests (one 404, one error): the results are in the order of the list, and the log has `http_all limit=2` and then the requests in the order of the list. Run 17 (Design Q226): limit 0, the log has `limit=0` and the results are in the order of the list (the fake runs the requests in the order of the list at any limit). Runs 18 and 19 (R-AP34): sleep! writes `sleep <ms>` and waits for no time.
